 qhAMLF: { t: 'Queensland Historical Atlas. “Empire and agribusiness: the Australian Mercantile Land and Finance Company”.', u: 'https://www.qhatlas.com.au/empire-and-agribusiness-australian-mercantile-land-and-finance-company', short: 'Queensland Historical Atlas, AML&F', note: 'Says that by 1904 the company held 80 stations as security for loans, six in Queensland, after taking foreclosed land in the 1890s, and that it bought its first Queensland station, Retro, in 1906. The page timed out when fetched, so it was read as a search-tool excerpt.' },
